subtasks.description:
Modify `handleAgentContextExhausted()` in `internal/orchestrator/context_monitor.go` (line 308-322) to handle classifier agents specially.

Current code:
```go
func (o *Orchestrator) handleAgentContextExhausted(subtask *model.Task, ag *model.Agent, pct int) error {
    ag.Status = model.AgentDead
    ag.CurrentTaskID = nil
    if err := o.db.Save(ag).Error; err != nil { ... }
    phase := o.getTaskPhase(subtask)
    if phase == "test" {
        return o.handleTestWritingFailure(subtask, ag)
    }
    return o.failTask(subtask, fmt.Sprintf("agent exhausted context window (%d%%)", pct))
}
```

Add a classifier check AFTER the agent save and BEFORE the phase check (after line 315). Insert:
```go
if ag.AgentType == model.AgentClassifier {
    return o.parkClassifierForTriage(subtask, fmt.Sprintf(
        "classifier agent %s exhausted context window at %d%%", ag.ID, pct))
}
```

This routes classifier context exhaustion to the existing `parkClassifierForTriage()` function in `classifying.go` (line 162), which sets `human_triage=true` and `classifier_error` — keeping the task in CLASSIFYING for human review rather than transitioning to FAILED.

Also add classifier handling in `checkContextUsage()` (line 111-131). Currently classifiers have no phase (empty string), so they skip the fixer threshold entirely and only hit the hard stop. Add a check at the start of the `pct >= o.contextFixerPct` block (before line 113):
```go
if ag.AgentType == model.AgentClassifier {
    // Classifiers at 85%+ are over-exploring — stop early.
    if err := o.runner.StopAgent(ag.ID); err != nil {
        o.logger.Error("checkContextUsage: stop classifier", "agent_id", ag.ID, "error", err)
        continue
    }
    if err := o.handleAgentContextExhausted(&subtask, &ag, pct); err != nil {
        o.logger.Error("checkContextUsage: handle classifier exhausted", "agent_id", ag.ID, "error", err)
    }
    continue
}
```

This stops classifiers at the fixer threshold (85%) instead of waiting for the hard stop (90%), since classifiers shouldn't need that much context.

Do NOT modify any test files.
